  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\nIssued at 1251 PM CDT MON AUG 10 2026\n\nThe \"copy/paste\" forecast will continue through Wednesday, as an\nupper-level ridge slowly slides west along the Gulf Coast.\nHowever, it appears as if the pattern will begin to change for\nthe worse by Thursday, as this upper-level ridge will begin to\nstrengthen. Initially, the center of this ridge will be somewhere\nin the vicinity of the Mississippi Delta region, generally ebbing\nand flowing east/west into the weekend. By the weekend proper\nhowever, the center of the ridge will anchor itself somewhere\nnear Arkansas, strengthening into next week.\n\nLocally, this will allow for afternoon high temperatures to\nsteadily climb into the weekend, with some locations reaching\nHeat Advisory criteria by Wednesday. Ambient temperatures will\nreach the mid to upper-90s by Friday, with mostly upper-90s\nexpected through the weekend. Given the high humidity, heat\nindices of 105-110 should become more widespread resulting in\nmedium to high (50-80%) chances for extended heat headlines into\nnext week.\n\n/44/",
